  "term": "ontology",
  "definition": "Ontology is the branch of philosophy concerned with reality or being in its most basic and ultimate sense. In historical usage, it shifted from meaning a general theory of being to, in more critical thought, the study of reality as it can be known, in contrast with the study of knowing itself.",
